  "title": "Accessible name and role",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## A button should be a button\n\nA `div` with a click is a trap for keyboard and screen readers. Use `<button>`. The **accessible name** is often the text content, or `aria-label`.\n\nSet the button’s label to `Call north` using `textContent` — not `innerHTML` for this plain phrase."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "div-click",
      "promptMd": "A `div` with `onclick` is a good button?",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "yes",
          "md": "Yes — click is enough"
        },
        {
          "id": "no",
          "md": "No — it misses role, keyboard, and name by default"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "no"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "name-button",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `#call` is a button. Set its accessible name (text) to `Call north`.",
      "preview": {
        "kind": "iframe"
      },
